BT /F1 10 Tf 50 720 Td (IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
AT NEW DELHI

CASE NO: Civil Appeal No. 2981 of 2026
CNR NUMBER: SCIN010023452026
DECISION DATE: 2026-02-18
YEAR: 2026

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Justice Sanjiv Khanna & Justice Dipankar Datta

PARTIES:
State Bank of India \(Lead Financial Creditor\)
... Appellant\(s\) / Petitioner\(s\)
Versus
Consortium of Resolution Applicants & Ors.
... Respondent\(s\) / State

STATUTORY PROVISIONS & ACTS REFERRED:
Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code 2016

SECTIONS & CLAUSES UNDER CONSIDERATION:
IBC Section 30\(4\), IBC Section 31, IBC Section 53

KEY LEGAL DOMAINS & TOPICS:
IBC, Commercial Wisdom, Committee of Creditors, Resolution Plan, NCLAT Jurisdiction

================================================================================
                                   JUDGMENT
================================================================================

1. FACTUAL MATRIX:
NCLAT interfered with the resolution plan approved by 88% majority of Committee of Creditors on grounds of equitable distribution to operational creditors.

2. ISSUES FRAMED FOR ADJUDICATION:
1. Is the commercial wisdom of Committee of Creditors subject to judicial review by NCLT/NCLAT on grounds of equity?

3. STATUTORY FRAMEWORK & PRECEDENTS:
Reaffirming Essar Steel and K. Sashidhar: CoC commercial wisdom is non-justiciable provided statutory requirements of Section 30\(2\) are satisfied.

4. RATIO DECIDENDI:
Judicial review of resolution plan approved by Committee of Creditors is limited strictly to Section 30\(2\) IBC compliance; adjudicating authorities cannot substitute their business judgment.

5. FINAL DISPOSITION & ORDER:
Civil Appeal Allowed; NCLAT order setting aside CoC approval quashed; Commercial wisdom of CoC upheld.

Decreed and ordered accordingly.

Hon'ble Justice Sanjiv Khanna & Justice Dipankar Datta
Supreme Court of India
